00:55:39,130 --> 00:55:45,130
Live Free or Die Hard (released as Die Hard 4.0 outside North America) is a
2007 American action thriller film directed by Len Wiseman.

11
01:01:13,043 --> 01:01:19,043
It is the sequel to Die Hard with a Vengeance (1995) and the
fourth installment in the Die Hard film series.

12
01:06:46,956 --> 01:06:52,956
It is based on the 1997 article "A Farewell to Arms"
written for Wired magazine by John Carlin.

13
01:12:20,869 --> 01:12:26,869
The film's name references New Hampshire's state motto, "Live Free or Die".

14
01:17:54,782 --> 01:18:00,782
In the film, NYPD Detective John McClane (Bruce Willis) attempts to stop a cyber-terrorist, Thomas Gabriel (Timothy Olyphant) who hacks into government and commercial
computers across the United States with the goal of starting a "fire sale" cyber attack that would disable key elements of the nation's infrastructure.

15
01:23:28,695 --> 01:23:34,695
Justin Long, Cliff Curtis, Maggie Q, Mary Elizabeth
Winstead and Kevin Smith also star.

16
01:29:02,608 --> 01:29:08,608
Live Free or Die Hard was released in the United States
on June 27, 2007 by 20th Century Fox.

17
01:34:36,521 --> 01:34:42,521
The film grossed $388 million worldwide, making it the
highest-grossing installment in the Die Hard series.

18
01:40:10,434 --> 01:40:16,434
It received positive reviews from critics.

19
01:45:44,347 --> 01:45:50,347
It is the only Die Hard film to be theatrically released with a PG-13 rating from the MPAA,
although an unrated edition would later be made available on home media.

20
